{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\fs24\b\fs32 VITL Stakeholder System Summary\b0\fs24\parStakeholder-facing summary\par\par\b Executive Summary\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab VITL is a MetaDyn medical simulation experience where a learner communicates with the mother of an infant patient in a guided pediatric UTI scenario.\par\tab\bullet\tab The product is moving beyond a simple AI conversation into a structured simulation with activity progression, communication scoring, and planned patient-history capture.\par\par\b Why It Matters\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab VITL demonstrates a higher-value MetaDyn product direction: scenario-driven immersive training that combines AI interaction with explicit simulation-state control.\par\tab\bullet\tab This creates a path toward more credible teaching, review, and assessment workflows over time.\par\par\b Current Milestone\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab The current milestone is to validate a working learner loop from greeting and rapport into structured patient-history intake.\par\tab\bullet\tab The first milestone is intentionally bounded to prove the experience flow before expanding into heavier assessment or reporting capabilities.\par\par\b System Components\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab Voice/controller layer for text, voice, transcription, model responses, and speech output.\par\tab\bullet\tab Simulation manager for activity flow, state, scoring hooks, escalation, and hidden scenario context.\par\tab\bullet\tab Communication scoring service for rubric-based learner scoring.\par\tab\bullet\tab Planned patient-intake layer for structured documentation of learner-collected history.\par\par\b Bottom Line\b0\par\tab\bullet\tab The near-term value is a coherent simulation loop where communication quality affects progression and structured history capture begins to look like a real training product instead of a chatbot demo.\par\par}